The root cause is in `pandas/io/formats/xml.py`, in `_BaseXMLFormatter._build_attribs` and `_build_elems`. Both call plain `str(...)` on the cell value, which turns Python bools into `"True"`/`"False"` instead of the `xs:boolean` literals `"true"`/`"false"`.

A minimal fix is to special-case bools before falling back to `str()`:

```python
@final
def _get_xml_value(self, val: Any) -> str:
    if isinstance(val, bool):
        return "true" if val else "false"
    return str(val)
```

and use it in both places instead of the bare `str(...)` call:

```python
    @final
    def _build_attribs(self, d: dict[str, Any], elem_row: Any) -> Any:
        ...
        for col in self.attr_cols:
            attr_name = self._get_flat_col_name(col)
            try:
                if not isna(d[col]):
                    elem_row.attrib[attr_name] = self._get_xml_value(d[col])
            except KeyError as err:
                raise KeyError(f"no valid column, {col}") from err
        return elem_row
```

```python
    @final
    def _build_elems(self, d: dict[str, Any], elem_row: Any) -> None:
        ...
        for col in self.elem_cols:
            elem_name = self._get_flat_col_name(col)
            try:
                val = None if isna(d[col]) or d[col] == "" else self._get_xml_value(d[col])
                sub_element_cls(elem_row, elem_name).text = val
            except KeyError as err:
                raise KeyError(f"no valid column, {col}") from err
```
